back here at home losing a loved one to  covet is never easy and fema's funeral  assistance is meant to ease financial  burden on families but as mary jane  bellieso shares some people may not know  they qualify for these benefits  when patrick cassell lost his mother to  covid in december 2020. he applied for  fema's funeral assistance program but  had a tough time completing the  application sometimes the paperwork is a  little more tedious and if we can get  help from a funeral home that would be  awesome because we all need help when it  comes to filling out government  paperwork that's the key fema's funeral  assistance provides up to nine thousand  dollars in burial cremation and eligible  services to qualified families who lost  a loved one due to covet 19. laura  sussman is a funeral director at kraft  sussman funeral and cremation services  she says filling out paperwork can be  intimidating for those already dealing  with grief and most people are shocked  they didn't know that it was available  or the government was doing that for  them but this doesn't have to be done  right away  so people could take their time they  have to wait until they get the death  certificate you know wait until all of  their funeral expenses are incurred  because  like some people at the beginning of  covet couldn't even do a service they  you know they were postponing that  so if they file you only get one chance  to file so if they file before they have  all their costs involved they're not  going to get reimbursed for the  additional costs casale hopes to provide  a bigger and proper service for his  mother in the future after covet limited  gatherings he says in the meantime he's  going to try applying again you know  when you're dealing with somebody's  death i mean we would have talked a year  ago or maybe 15 months ago i don't know  how or not 12 months ago yeah about a  year ago i don't know how receptive i  would be now a year later  um things are more digested and you know  you live with it now is a good time to  probably want to apply mary jane bella  live local now  well to apply for this relief you will  need proof of funeral expenses an  official death certificate listing covet  19 as the cause of death and you must  disclose any funds received specifically  for funeral costs and will offset the  fema benefits
 

